<p>According to the description on SCP-871's page:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If any of these cakes is substantially damaged through any means other than being eaten by a human, including being eaten by a non-human animal, it will be replaced instantaneously.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Thus, if you were to try to feed 871 to 3048, you would get spontaneous cake combustion and a brand new instance of Keter pastry.</p>
<p>Something I find equally entertaining is the thought of cross-testing SCP-3048 with <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-504">SCP-504</a>.</p>

